WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:08.620
Stepping out on
an ordinary Sunday

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:15.130
Stepping out!
A miracle's gonna happen

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:16.960
It's my day!

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:27.540
Maybe I'll throw off my pajamas

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:34.950
and head out to see her right now

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:42.320
I always turned my eyes away,
thinking she'd hate me

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:49.730
Now I'm saying goodbye
to that negative attitude

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:55.500
My favorite shoes
will always take me

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.640
To a place where I'll be happy

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:10.150
It's not someone else
I want to embrace

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:16.290
But a version of
myself that's not fake

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:19.360
I just want to walk

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.890
Not on tip-toe

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:26.860
Not downcast, either

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:35.770
Just I'm stepping out
on an ordinary Sunday

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:42.210
Stepping out!
Making a little try, try, try

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.480
It's my day!

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:50.150
He got on the wrong plane and
landed in Vancouver?

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:54.960
He'll lend you a million yen,
if you come and get him?

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.430
It's just like him.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.570
It's not funny!
How do I get to Canada?

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.770
I'm broke, as it is.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:18.680
Going to get him might be
a good excuse to go to Canada.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:21.420
That's right.
And he has a villa there.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:22.520
You're right.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:27.590
Makino, you can invite
a friend along, too.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:29.090
What are you talking...?

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.160
Yeah! And the snow
in Canada's great.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:32.560
Shall we go snowboarding?

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:33.990
Yeah! This is gonna be fun.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:37.030
Wait a minute!
Did you hear what I said?

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:54.080
"Tsukushi Goes to Canada!!"

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.600
<i>Why does it always
happen like this?!</i>

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:15.100
Tsukushi... Are those all
Eitoku students?

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.840
They look so mature
and high class...

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:22.110
<i>They didn't invite
just my friend along.</i>

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:25.510
<i>Why do I have to be on this plane
with Asai and her gang?</i>

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.680
<i>My life is cursed!</i>

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:33.890
Nishikado... What's this all about?
How could you invite <i>them</i>?

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:37.220
Huh? Didn't you invite them?

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:39.860
I don't know about them. Really.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:42.890
Makino...

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.000
Don't be negative.
Let's just enjoy ourselves.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.740
Sakurako? You're here too?

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:54.240
What's with that
"pure and innocent" hairstyle?

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:59.380
Please! Don't be so sarcastic!
Aren't we friends?

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:02.980
Never mind that.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:08.520
I heard Domyoji said
he'd lend you a million yen...

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:11.890
if you went to get him
in Vancouver.

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:16.530
Nice work.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.340
How did you hear that?

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.870
<i>Oh, the future looks bleak...</i>

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:47.760
Tsukasa's villa is about
a 3-hour drive from here.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:52.630
The air is so fresh!
Isn't this exciting?

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.600
Yes. You're right.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.730
It's silly to say this, but
there are so many foreigners here.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:01.240
That's why I hate poor folk.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.340
It's probably their first
overseas trip.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:09.010
Did someone say something
about poor folk?

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.710
No, of course not!
Look! Isn't that guy handsome?

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:13.920
Where?

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:18.490
<i>This is bad. Yuki is so innocent.</i>

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:22.260
<i>If they sink their fangs into her,
she'll be a goner.</i>

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.960
<i>I've got to protect her!</i>

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:31.780
Hey, you guys...
How long are you going to follow us?

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:35.370
We're going to Tsukasa's villa.
Go away!

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:36.780
What?

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.110
<i>Good for you, Nishikado!</i>

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.910
But... we...

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:44.040
<i>Yeah... Get lost!</i>

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.290
Makino invited us, after all!

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.580
What?!

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:52.390
We came because she begged us.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.050
So you did invite them.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.140
I did...

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:01.930
He's got about 50 bedrooms,
so it should be all right.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:03.440
N-no...

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.810
What happened, Tsukushi?

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:14.470
N-nothing...

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:19.020
- Isn't it wonderful?
- I'm so happy.

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:39.900
What a beautiful villa!

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:44.500
Wow...

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.510
Hey, Tsukasa!

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:58.620
Tsukasa! Are you here?

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:03.950
Isn't he here? It's cold.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:07.160
I think the room at the far end
has a fireplace.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:12.960
Huh?

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.770
So, you are here.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:17.670
Yo!

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:19.870
Thanks for having us.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:23.350
What are they doing here?

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.360
I don't know. They tagged along.

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:34.950
So you came after all, pauper.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.390
How do you like
your first overseas trip?

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:40.220
It's the pits!

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.060
What?

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.370
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:00.790
I had to come because
I had to help my family.

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:05.780
More importantly, you are keeping
your promise, aren't you?

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:07.080
Of course!

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:10.570
Do you think I would be troubled
over small change?

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:16.090
Anyway, you said you wouldn't
be returning for a while...

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:17.810
You're so weak-willed!

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:19.580
What?

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.900
You swaggered and said
you were going to New York.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:26.170
Then you get on the wrong plane
and end up in Canada.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:28.140
Who's the big fool here?

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:43.850
Listen, we came all the way
to Canada to get you...

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:46.850
so why don't we try to get along.
Right? Right?

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:14.250
Ouch!

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.150
Pretty bad, Tsukushi.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:23.160
Can it! How can you expect me
to slide on a piece of wood?

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:24.960
Where are the canes?

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:27.480
They're not canes,
they're ski poles.

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:30.830
Everybody snowboards, nowadays.

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:32.620
Don't give up!

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:35.830
Damn them!
They do it like it's nothing.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.400
They could've helped me up.

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:38.900
Damn!

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.030
<i>Pretty cool!</i>

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:00.430
What are you laughing about?

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:12.500
LOUSY... FOOL?

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:14.710
I'm a lousy fool?

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:20.180
What... You came all this way
just to show me that?

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:21.610
You're the fool!

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:25.020
What's wrong with saying
you're lousy, if you are?

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:28.050
If you don't like it,
see if you can catch me.

00:10:28.550 --> 00:10:32.520
Just wait and see. This is easy
if you set your mind to it.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.130
Who's lousy?!

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:44.030
I'll get you for this!

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:55.550
Got it!

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:02.850
After all that...

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:06.540
You're pretty good.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:07.160
Huh?

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:10.360
You can have that. Isn't it fun?

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:12.260
What is it?

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:15.920
I got it at the airport toy shop.
Not bad, huh?

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:19.700
The toy shop?
You're like a child.

00:11:23.340 --> 00:11:25.430
Hey, Yuriko... Look at that.

00:12:18.530 --> 00:12:23.320
Domyoji is so intense, isn't he?
Even though he's so handsome.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.070
Handsome? You're kidding.

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:27.900
He is handsome.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:31.370
The other three, too.
You don't often see boys like them.

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:35.340
Ow! My scrapes sting.

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:40.210
Imagine having a hot spring
in your basement...

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:45.080
There really are people in this world
with villas like this.

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:50.990
Even if he has money,
it means nothing if he's rotten inside.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:54.230
But I go to a public
high school, you know?

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:56.360
You can't find a single boy
like them.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:58.600
I envy you.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:02.530
<i>What kind of reaction is that?</i>

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:05.970
What's this?

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:11.110
Oh...

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:29.560
It's like a movie.

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:32.260
What?

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.600
It's on your face.

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:37.630
That did it! OK, it's <i>on</i>!

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:42.540
Come on, stop that, Yuki.

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:52.420
It's been so long...
since we took a trip together.

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:55.420
Not since the class trip 
in eighth grade.

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:56.020
Yeah.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:14:00.020
Chimura and Aki said
they missed you.

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:04.430
That takes me back! How are they?

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:06.460
The same as usual.

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:17.040
<i>I'm glad...</i>

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:20.040
<i>Yuki's here with me.</i>

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:25.280
<i>That's right... We should enjoy ourselves
while we're here.</i>

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:31.050
<i>It'll be back to harsh reality
when I return to Japan.</i>

00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:40.400
Tsukushi... I'll meet you
up in our room.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:41.500
Okay.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:52.710
Yuki...

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:55.470
Huh?

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:03.450
Yuki!

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:05.290
Yuki!

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:09.490
Yuki?

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:18.600
No way...

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.400
- It's true.
- It's the fad.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:22.600
That's strange...
Where did she go?

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:25.510
Oh, Rui Hanazawa!

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:27.310
Have you seen Yuki?

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:28.510
Who's that?

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:34.280
My friend!
She came with me, remember?

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:35.180
I don't know.

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:38.690
If you're looking for your friend...

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:42.550
She went out a while ago
for another run.

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:46.090
Another run?

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:52.530
But it's a blizzard out there.

00:15:56.340 --> 00:15:58.400
You didn't do something
to her, did you?

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:03.410
What a thing to say!
Did you hear her, Hanazawa?

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:04.410
Shut up!

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:13.950
Makino!

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:27.330
Yuki!

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.000
Yuki!

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:34.910
Yuki!

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:40.140
<i>What should I do?
If anything should happen to Yuki...</i>

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:44.180
Hey... Give me the car keys.

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:45.980
Oh, Hanazawa...

00:16:46.550 --> 00:16:48.190
What's the matter?
You look pale...

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:56.430
Did you, by any chance,
come with Makino?

00:16:58.430 --> 00:16:59.530
That's right...

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:02.000
You're Yuki?

00:17:03.400 --> 00:17:03.970
Yes.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:08.640
<i>She went out a while ago
for another run.</i>

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:17.380
<i>The snow is stinging my face.
I can't breathe.</i>

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:22.520
<i>Did Yuki really say
she was going out?</i>

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:28.660
Yuki!

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:33.030
Yuki!

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:36.430
Yuki!

00:17:42.970 --> 00:17:47.580
<i>If she gets caught out here,
she'll freeze to death!</i>

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:49.610
<i>I've got to find her quickly!</i>

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:52.580
Ouch!

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:56.550
My leg's caught in the snow.

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:00.320
I sprained my ankle...

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:04.360
Ow...

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.250
I can't see the lights.

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:37.420
I came from that way...

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:39.930
No, maybe this way.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.060
<i>All I can see is snow.</i>

00:18:44.630 --> 00:18:50.600
<i>Don't tell me I... I... I'm lost!</i>

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:11.120
Rui...

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:15.390
I really did think she went out!

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:16.900
Liar!

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:21.170
This is the only villa around here.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:24.640
If she gets lost...

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:30.210
...she'll die.

00:19:54.970 --> 00:19:55.730
Tsukushi...

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:06.510
Did something happen to Makino?

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:35.270
It's cold...

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:40.440
Do I have anything...
to warm me up?

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:53.230
"LOUSY FOOL"

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:01.900
<i>I can't feel my hands or feet.</i>

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:11.840
<i>My head is fuzzy... I can't move...</i>

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:19.050
<i>Am I going to... die?</i>

00:22:05.930 --> 00:22:12.000
You let your hair down a little

00:22:13.970 --> 00:22:19.870
You hid the fact
that you were crying

00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:29.750
I noticed, but I
couldn't ask you why

00:22:29.980 --> 00:22:37.790
I can never be
honest about how I feel

00:22:37.790 --> 00:22:45.560
Until after we've split
up after a bad fight

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:53.710
I can say it now,
though, over and over

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:53.710
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:22:53.710 --> 00:23:02.080
I can say "I love you"...

00:22:53.710 --> 00:23:02.080
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:03.880 --> 00:23:11.860
Do you really hate me this time?

00:23:11.860 --> 00:23:19.630
Will you end up running to him?

00:23:19.900 --> 00:23:27.800
I can say it now,
though, over and over

00:23:19.900 --> 00:23:27.800
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:36.210
I can say "I love you"...

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:36.210
(Sorry girl, I was
wrong and I love you)

00:23:48.420 --> 00:23:50.790
I ran out into the blizzard...

00:23:51.130 --> 00:23:52.960
to save my precious friend.

00:23:53.660 --> 00:23:56.570
Domyoji ran out into the blizzard...

00:23:57.770 --> 00:23:58.730
for whom?

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:02.710
Hana Yori Dango:
"His Body Against Mine!"

00:24:03.570 --> 00:24:05.370
I haven't been honest
with my feelings...

00:24:05.740 --> 00:24:08.710
but his warmth
comes through to me.
